 ],
 "literal": "Hanging-root-low screw-pine's mature thick bud / like a preening heron's feather expanding, its petals open / in the front yard of the small hamlet close to the seashore grove, / where waves come and return, they say, having abandoned us / though he is of a very far country, / he is close to the heart, in the cool sea land.",
 "translation": "In the front yard of our small hamlet near the seashore grove, where waves come and go, the mature, thick buds of the screw-pine with low-hanging roots open their petals like the preening feathers of a heron. They say he has abandoned us and gone to a very distant land; yet, he of the cool sea land remains close to my heart.",
 "modern": "விழுதுகள் தாழ்ந்த தாழையின் முதிர்ந்த பருத்த மொட்டு, நாரை தன் சிறகை விரிப்பது போல இதழ்கள் அவிழ்ந்து மலரும். கடற்கரைச் சோலையை அடுத்த நம் சிறு குடிலின் முற்றத்தில் அலைகள் வந்து வந்து மீளும். நம்மைத் துறந்து அவர் மிகத் தொலைதூர நாட்டிற்குச் சென்றுவிட்டார் என்று கூறுகிறார்கள். ஆயினும், குளிர்ந்த கடல் நாட்டை உடைய அவர் என் நெஞ்சிற்கு மிக நெருக்கமானவராகவே இருக்கிறார்.",
 "explanation": "The heroine (thalaivi) is speaking to her friend (thōḻi) about the hero (thalaivaṉ) who has gone away to a distant land. Although others say he has abandoned her, she feels his constant presence in her heart. The poem is set in the Neytal (seashore) landscape, characterized by the screw-pine (tāḻai) blooming in the front yard of the coastal hamlet where waves constantly come and go. The image of the screw-pine bud opening like a heron preening its feathers evokes the beauty and intimacy of their coastal home. The coming and going of the waves symbolizes the constant flow of her thoughts of him, showing that despite the physical distance, he remains close to her heart.",
